// Cycle of Life: Realistic Fauna - FotSA civets, genets and relatives (Viverridae Plus).
//
// 35 small carnivorans: fifteen genets, two oyans, the Asian and African civets, the palm civets and
// the binturong, three invertebrate specialists, the semi-aquatic otter civet, and the African palm
// civet - which despite its name is not a viverrid at all but the only living member of Nandiniidae.
//
// Almost everything here is inherited and correct. Weights are declared per species and accurate
// across the range, from a 700 g oyan to a 15 kg binturong. Group sizes are 1 throughout (2.5 for
// the otter civet), which is right for a family of solitary nocturnal animals. Spawn blocks are
// land-only, so even the otter civet places safely. And there is no predator-misclassification risk:
// these carry no "predator" tag, so the tagged-predator fallback cannot fire on them the way it does
// on the Tasmanian devil.
//
// The mod also splits diets thoughtfully already - Hose's civet and the two oyans get Protein only
// (correctly leaving them outside the forage model), while most of the family gets Fruit + Protein,
// of which only Fruit is a plant category here.
//
// TWO CHANGES:
//
// 1. K, 6 -> 1 (2 for the common palm civets). Six per 0.173 km² reads as ~35 animals/km². Genets
//    run 1-3/km², most civets around 1, and the binturong well below that. The Asian palm civets are
//    the exception - genuinely common, often living alongside people, and dense enough in fruiting
//    forest to justify 2.
//
// 2. THE CARNIVOROUS ONES STOP BEING FRUIT FORAGERS. The mod gives most of the family Fruit, which
//    is right for the palm civets, the binturong, the omnivorous Viverra civets and Nandinia - all
//    genuine fruit-eaters and seed dispersers. It is not right for the GENETS, which live on rodents,
//    birds and insects and take fruit only incidentally; nor for the banded palm civet, which despite
//    its name eats invertebrates; nor for the otter civet, which catches fish and frogs. Those
//    seventeen get isForager false, which leaves them as pure population dynamics - the same
//    treatment this pack already gives vipers, pangolins, kiwi and adzebills, all animals whose real
//    food (insects, worms, rodents) this model does not track. Better to represent that honestly than
//    to file a rodent-hunter under fruit.
//
// No territory entries. These are small solitary animals with home ranges rather than defended
// ground, and at K=1 a radius below the founding radius would change nothing in any case.
//
// VERIFICATION STATUS: keys derived from the mod's own entity JSON, not read off a live roster -
// this mod is not installed on the pack author's server. A wrong key is inert (the entry is ignored
// and the animal keeps its auto-discovered values); `/col species` lists the authoritative keys.
